===========================================================================
PARITY NOTES (web KioskOverlay.tsx → native)
===========================================================================
  KioskOverlay is a PURE presentational overlay — it receives config + flags as
  props and fetches nothing (its only hooks are useTranslation [i18n facade] and
  useDateFormat [formatters], neither of which is networking). So the prompt's
  loading/empty/error/stale/offline states are the EMBEDDING Kiosk page's concern,
  not the overlay's; the branches the web source ACTUALLY carries are reproduced
  here in full and unit-tested (same disposition as the merged P-0073-BatteryPill
  and the web ToolCard/pill components):

  • dim layer    web `isDimmed && <div bg-black style{opacity:1-dimLevel}>` →
                 Color.black.opacity(dimOpacity), allowsHitTesting(false),
                 ignoresSafeArea. dimOpacity = clamp(1-dimLevel, 0…1); a non-finite
                 dimLevel ⇒ 0 (never blacks out the screen). Verified 0.5⇒0.5,
                 0⇒1, 1⇒0, 1.5⇒0, −0.5⇒1, NaN/±Inf⇒0.
  • cursor hide  web `isCursorHidden` injects `cursor:none` → .kioskPointerHidden
                 modifier hides the macOS pointer (NSCursor) on hover; a correct
                 no-op on touch platforms (no system pointer). Decision tested via
                 presentation.hidesPointer.
  • clock        web `showClock` + `clockPosition` (4 corners) + formatTime/
                 formatDateWithDay, ticking each second → TimelineView(.periodic
                 by:1); KioskClockPosition.alignment maps to .top/bottomLeading/
                 Trailing; KioskClock ports use setLocalizedDateFormatFromTemplate
                 "jjmm" / "EEEMMMd" so a 24h locale yields "14:30" and a 12h locale
                 "02:30 PM" / "Sat, Apr 4" from the same call (locale-aware, like
                 toLocale*String). text-2xl mono + tabular digits → 24pt monospaced;
                 text-[var(--text-muted)] → Color.TS.textMuted.
  • rotation     web `dashboardCount > 1 && rotateInterval > 0` indicator dots,
                 active `w-6` vs inactive `w-1.5`, both `bg-[var(--surface-2)]` →
                 Capsule fill Color.TS.surface, width 24 vs 6, height 6; the gate +
                 active-dot test reproduce the web exactly (count=1⇒hidden,
                 interval=0⇒hidden, count≥2&interval>0⇒shown). eased width change
                 gated on reduce-motion.
  • exit         web ghost `Button` (X + "Exit Kiosk"), `bg-[var(--surface-overlay)]
                 backdrop-blur-sm`, fades in on mousemove/touchstart, hides after
                 3000ms; aria-label `kiosk.exit` → TSButton(.ghost,.small) with the
                 icon+label foregrounded text-secondary, .ultraThinMaterial glass
                 chip, top-trailing; reveal on tap/hover via an interaction sensor,
                 auto-hide after KioskOverlayExit.autoHideDelay (= .seconds(3),
                 tested) re-armed by an interaction token + .task(id:). The chip
                 stays accessibility-visible (and focusable) while VoiceOver runs so
                 it can never become unreachable. accessibilityLabel = "Exit kiosk
                 mode" (web aria-label), visible text = "Exit Kiosk".
  • tokens map   --text-muted→textMuted, --text-secondary→textSecondary,
                 --surface-2→Color.TS.surface, --surface-overlay+blur→ultraThinMaterial.
  • i18n         every t()/aria string resolves through KioskOverlayStrings (P1/S10
                 table "KioskOverlay") with the web English literal as the fallback;
                 zero hardcoded user-facing literals in code.
  • a11y         clock = one combined element labelled "Time <t>, <date>"; dots =
                 ignored children labelled "Dashboard X of Y"; dim is hidden;
                 exit carries an explicit label + .isButton; Dynamic Type preview;
                 reduce-motion honored on dim/dots/exit animations.

